---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="WayTutor privacy policy"
  description="Which data WayTutor processes, for what purpose, for how long and with whom it is shared."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="section policy">
    <h1>WayTutor privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="version">Version 2, November 8th, 2026.</p>

    <p>
      WayTutor is a Chrome extension that reads your academic portal material aloud and
      generates a spoken summary of it. This page describes which data the service
      processes, for what purpose, for how long and with whom it is shared.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      WayTutor is operated by Márcio Júnior, a Waypoint Labs project. The contact for
      any matter in this policy, including deletion requests, is
      <a href="mailto:privacidade@marcio.run">privacidade@marcio.run</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Which data we process</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Data</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Google account identifier, e-mail, name and profile photo URL</td>
          <td>To identify who is using the service and grant access. The photo is not displayed anywhere today.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Text of the material passages, during reading</td>
          <td>To generate the audio and the summary. It is the content the extension sent from the open page.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Generated audio</td>
          <td>To be played and reused when someone else reads the same passage.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Usage counters: synthesized characters and summaries per month and per day</td>
          <td>To enforce the monthly limit and estimate the cost of the service.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Access record: session creation and last-use dates, browser identifier</td>
          <td>To keep the login for up to 7 days and allow revoking access.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      The material text is not stored as text. What remains is the audio generated from
      it and the counters. The password of your Google account never reaches us: sign-in
      happens at Google itself.
    </p>

    <h2>What we keep in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      The extension keeps the access token, your preferences (voice, favorite voices,
      speed and figure pause) and the reading position of each material in Chrome local
      storage. We use no cookies, we do not track browsing and we do not read pages
      outside portal addresses.
    </p>

    <h2>With whom we share</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google</strong>, to authenticate your account and to convert text into speech.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Vercel AI Gateway</strong>, which forwards the text to the model
        providers in use: Google, for the voice, and OpenAI, for the summary. These
        providers process the text to return the audio or the summary.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which stores the audio files.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Discord</strong>, which receives a technical alert when a request fails:
        the route, the status code and the duration, with no user data.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Fly.io</strong>, hosting the server, and <strong>Neon</strong>, hosting the database.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not sell data, we do not use your data for advertising and we do not share
      it with third parties for their own purposes. Use of data obtained through the
      Google APIs follows the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the
      Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Transfer outside Brazil</h2>
    <p>
      The providers above process data in other countries, mainly the United States.
      The transfer happens to perform the service you requested, under article 33 of
      the LGPD.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account and counters: while the account exists.</li>
      <li>Access session: 7 days, renewed at each use, closed on logout.</li>
      <li>Login code: 2 minutes, single use.</li>
      <li>
        Audio: indefinitely. The file is identified by a code computed from the text,
        the voice and the model, not by account, so the cache does not record who
        listened to what.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can request confirmation of processing, access, correction, anonymization,
      portability, deletion of the data and revocation of consent. Just write to
      <a href="mailto:privacidade@marcio.run">privacidade@marcio.run</a>. We answer
      within 15 days. Deleting the account removes access, sessions and counters;
      audio already generated stays in the cache, because it cannot be linked to a
      person.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      All traffic uses HTTPS. The access token is stored on the server only as a hash,
      and each account is manually approved. Access can be paused or revoked at any
      time.
    </p>

    <h2>Children and teenagers</h2>
    <p>
      The service is meant for higher education students and is not directed at anyone
      under 18.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>When processing changes, this page is updated and the date at the top moves with it.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
